   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "record UNCERTAINTY, return 503\n-> a recovery worker resolves it by READING\napplied_legs on the partition.   The only safe move.",
   "originalText": "record UNCERTAINTY, return 503\n-> a recovery worker resolves it by READING\napplied_legs on the partition.   The only safe move.",
   "fontSize": 12,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "center",
   "verticalAlign": "middle",
   "containerId": "t3",
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "tn",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 30,
   "y": 548,
   "width": 1011,
   "height": 48,
   "strokeColor": "#1e40af",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100059,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700413,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "On timeout the coordinator does NOT know whether the leg applied - the request may have committed and the response been lost.\nThis is why partitions expose idempotency on (transaction_id, leg_number) rather than the coordinator merely tracking its own\nattempts: the coordinator's memory of what it did is not trustworthy. The log is.",
   "originalText": "On timeout the coordinator does NOT know whether the leg applied - the request may have committed and the response been lost.\nThis is why partitions expose idempotency on (transaction_id, leg_number) rather than the coordinator merely tracking its own\nattempts: the coordinator's memory of what it did is not trustworthy. The log is.",
   "fontSize": 13,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
